cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  This software was developed for the paper listed under "references".
  If you use it, please cite both the software (Zenodo DOI of the version
  you used) and the paper.
type: software
title: "WCM_SWB_Irri: field-scale irrigation estimation with a soil water balance model coupled to the Water Cloud Model"
authors:
  - family-names: Natali
    given-names: Martina
    email: martinanatali@cnr.it
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.22961226
identifiers:
  - type: doi
    value: 10.5281/zenodo.22961226
    description: All versions (concept DOI)
  - type: doi
    value: 10.5281/zenodo.22961227
    description: Version 0.1.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/martina01natali/WCM_SWB_Irri"
license: GPL-3.0-only
version: 0.1.0
abstract: >-
  Per-field Bayesian (PyMC) calibration of a two-layer soil water balance
  model coupled to the Water Cloud Model against Sentinel-1 backscatter, with
  Sentinel-2 NDVI and meteorological data as inputs, to estimate irrigation
  from satellite data without in-situ measurements. Includes the scripts that download the input data
  (Sentinel-1/2 via Google Earth Engine, SoilGrids, MERIDA) and notebooks to
  analyse the results.
keywords:
  - irrigation
  - Sentinel-1
  - Sentinel-2
  - Water Cloud Model
  - soil water balance
  - Bayesian calibration
references:
  - type: article
    title: "Field-scale irrigation estimation using Sentinel-1 and Sentinel-2 data within a soil water balance model coupled to the Water Cloud Model"
